titre$ Key to the Resupinatus species recorded from South America
com$ adapt GF 05/2017
1,0$source : Georgea Santos Nogueira-Melo, Leif Ryvarden & Tatiana Baptista Gibertoni 2011 /// First record of Resupinatus poriaeformis (Agaricomycetes) from South America /// MYCOTAXON  Volume 117, pp. 423–427
1,0$
1,2 $ a. Hymenial surface lamellate
1,5 $ b. Hymenial surface smooth
2,0 $ a. Basidiomata reniform to flabelliform up to 2.5-4 cm $ R. dealbatus
2,3 $ b. Basidiomata cupulate to flabelliform up to 1 cm
3,0 $ a. Cystidial elements lacking $ R. graminum
3,4 $ b. Cystidial elements present
4,0 $ a. Basidiospores subglobose, 4-4.5 x 5 µm $ R. applicatus
4,0 $ a. Basidiospores ellipsoid to cylindrical, slightly curved 5.8-7.8 × 2.7-3.6 µm $ R. alboniger
5,0 $ a. Basidiospores globose to subglobose, 4.5 × 6 µm diam. $ R. poriaeformis
5,0 $ b. Basidiospores ellipsoid, 6-6.5 × 3.3-4 µm $ R. hyalinus

